---
import LegalLayout from '@layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '@data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title={`Privacy — ${site.name}`}
  description="How SGLA handles the information you share through this website."
  heading="Privacy"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>Who this covers</h2>
  <p>
    This notice explains what happens to information you share with {site.name} through
    <a href={site.url}>sgla.co.uk</a>. The data controller is {site.name}, contactable at
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you use the contact form, the details you enter (your name, business, email address,
    website address and message) are sent by email to {site.email} so that I can reply to you. The
    email is delivered through Resend, a transactional email service, which processes the message on
    my behalf. Submissions aren't stored in a database on this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    I keep these emails for as long as needed to answer your enquiry and, if we work together, for
    the duration of the project and a reasonable period afterwards for record-keeping. The legal
    basis for this is legitimate interest in responding to enquiries and, where relevant, taking
    steps to enter into a contract.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses Vercel Web Analytics to understand roughly how many people visit and which pages
    they look at. It doesn't use cookies, doesn't track you across other websites, and doesn't store
    personal data that identifies you. Because of this, there's no cookie banner.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel's servers process standard technical
    data such as IP addresses when delivering pages, in line with Vercel's own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under UK GDPR you can ask to see, correct or delete the personal information I hold about you.
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and I'll deal with it promptly. If
    you're not happy with how I've handled your data, you can complain to the Information
    Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this notice changes, the updated version will be published here with a new date.</p>
</LegalLayout>
